From e9422fd109912a59beac282668c6ce40088a4127 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:18:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Kanban owner probes: disposable host worker policy
 for the probe and its children

On a worker host (kanban.worker_resources.enabled in the account's ~/.hermes/config.yaml) the
three real-dispatcher probes failed at origin/main: test_kanban_restart_continuation (2 tests),
test_kanban_recovery (4) and test_session_kanban::test_real_dispatcher_lifecycle (4, file timeout).
CI hosts have no account policy, so they stayed green there.

Why:
1. worker_compute_capacity.policy_root() is the OS account's ~/.hermes by design (pwd, never HOME
   or HERMES_HOME). conftest patches it in the pytest process, but the probes run as subprocesses
   with a disposable HOME/HERMES_HOME, so they and their gateway owners read the real host policy.
2. The probe's dispatcher claim then registered its tmp board in the real account inventory, which
   10580b6996 refuses under test ("pytest must not register boards in the real account worker
   inventory (/home/ubuntu/.hermes)"): every claim failed and the probe hit
   "deadline: dispatcher claim and spawn".
3. With only the probe process isolated, the gateway owner still read the real policy and placed
   the card's worker in a CPU slice the disposable run never has ("Managed worker is outside its
   card CPU slice"), so the turn never reached the model ("model never reached").

Fix (tests only): local_recovery_probe.isolate_host_policy(home) points policy_root at
<home>/host-policy in the probe process and, through a fixtures/host_policy/sitecustomize.py on
the children's PYTHONPATH, in every Python child that imports worker_compute_capacity. Each
child that applies it drops a child-<pid> marker. The tests assert the receipt's policy_root is
under tmp_path and that the children (the restart test: each owner pid) read it, so dropping
either half turns them red on any host, not only on a worker.

Proof on hermes-worker-1 (live gateway + workers, worker_resources enabled):
- origin/main: 2 failed (restart_continuation), 4 failed (recovery), 4 failed (session_kanban).
- this change: 3 files, 43 passed.
- mutant without the children's hook: 6 failed + session_kanban file timeout.
- mutant without the probe-process patch: same 6 + timeout, 150 inventory refusals in the log.
